    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <tags>bitcraft bitcoin aml fraud-detection blockchain tui terminal cli</tags>
    <summary>Bitcoin transaction intelligence in your terminal.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
BitCraft ranks suspicious Bitcoin transactions and lets you investigate them in
the terminal: ranked alerts, provenance-tagged evidence, SHAP reasons and an
animated link-analysis view.

After installing, run `bitcraft` from any terminal to open it in a new, large
window. `bitcraft demo` uses built-in demo data; `bitcraft --help` lists the
other commands.

BitCraft connects to a BitCraft API at http://localhost:8000 (see the source
repository for the API and ML pipeline) and falls back to demo data when none
is running.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/RohanOnKeys/bitcraft/releases</releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="python3" version="3.10.0" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
